          "siteDescription": {
            "Description_en": "Dystric Planosols are seasonally ponded or saturated with water in the upper portion due to a slowly permeable, clay-rich subsoil. These soils are prone to compaction and require drainage for crop production. Dystric Planosols are less productive soils with low base saturation in the subsoil.",
